; SW-163: a QUOTED bignum-magnitude integer literal must read/print
; identically between native and the VM. Native's own quote lowering
; (lib/backend/llvm_codegen.cpp codegenQuotedAST) had no case for
; ESHKOL_BIGNUM_LITERAL and fell into `default`, silently returning null —
; `(car '(123456789012345678901234567890 1))` was `()`, `(exact?
; '123...)` was #f, `(number->string '123...)` printed "0". The VM's own
; quote lowering (lib/backend/vm_parser.c compile_quote()) already got this
; case right as part of SW-155.
;
; Deliberately NOT covered here (both still open, VM-side, unrelated to this
; fix): a quoted bignum-RATIONAL literal (VM's compile_quote() has no case
; for its own `(exact-rational n d)` rational-literal desugar, so `'1/3`
; still quotes to a 3-element list on the VM) and a bignum literal inside a
; quasiquote template (VM's compile_quasiquote() "Atom: number" arm ignores
; the is_bignum flag). Both are exercised, on native only, by
; tests/core/quoted_bignum_literals_test.esk.
(display (number->string '123456789012345678901234567890)) (newline)
(display (exact? '123456789012345678901234567890)) (newline)
(display (car '(123456789012345678901234567890 1))) (newline)
(display (cdr '(123456789012345678901234567890 1))) (newline)
(display (number->string '-123456789012345678901234567890)) (newline)
(display (exact? '-123456789012345678901234567890)) (newline)
(display (+ '123456789012345678901234567890 1)) (newline)
(display (vector? '#(1 123456789012345678901234567890 3))) (newline)
(display (vector-ref '#(1 123456789012345678901234567890 3) 1)) (newline)
(display (cdr '(1 . 123456789012345678901234567890))) (newline)
(display (equal? '123456789012345678901234567890 123456789012345678901234567890)) (newline)
